v:DAT-08 a v:Element, v:DataAsset ; v:identifier "DAT-08" ; v:label "| DAT-08 | Effects/receipts/operation outcomes / CMP-09 and host | General payloads may contain full content; native F13 receipts retain only original invocation/operation, native identity, historical membership and authored versions, never a root/body/target snapshot. Native result disclosure meets copied admission ceiling and current bound grant; eviction does not restore execution. F14 receipts retain only original decision/direction/target references under scoped grants; F06 observation contexts retain bounded copied metadata/projected signatures and owned reference/wait records, not separate historical roots; their parent authority handle keeps ancestor ownership/charges live until discharged. Wait termination does not discharge producer/provider ownership. Shared observation admission retains bounded reservation/context bindings, reusable charges and consumed quotas; observer stop is not shared discharge. Scoped clipboard cancellation preserves the accepted provider fact and separate local pin/provider obligation; local stop never implies provider quiescence. Owned F17 SaveAs receipts retain only invocation/status/operation/document under the lifecycle ceiling and current release; the private task-bound producer authority is not serialized or granted by that receipt. Owned initial-load F17 receipts additionally retain the exact created/joined/already-activated disposition; private read-task/codec/paired-writer authority is not serialized. Actual read retirement revokes that authority rather than retaining retired task records through its handle. Other late/unknown evidence retains its own bounded obligations |" ; v:status v:Modeled .
v:DAT-08 v:mentions v:CMP-09 .
