v:PS-UP a v:ProofSlice ; v:scope "Separate abstract closed backlog of two/three cooperative jobs, no arrivals/retries and finite cancellation/invalidation state. Under explicit weak fairness of service, all jobs acquire exactly one applied/superseded/cancelled disposition; cancellation alone does not discharge. Finite-state temporal checking has no transition-horizon cutoff. Not an implementation/refinement of a scheduler, open workloads, per-class service bounds, numeric SLO or arbitrary native-worker preemption." ; v:module "UsefulProgress" .
