v:ACS-02 a v:AssuranceClaim ; v:claimKind "BoundedSafety" ; v:claimText "A fixed recipient diagnostic projection masks modeled hidden existence and private identity differences and rechecks current release context after preparation." ; v:argument "Compose actual Disclosure steps with one prepare/drain pair, compare both recipient output sequences, and freeze delivery-time permission/epoch/disposal/hidden-divergence facts. Witnesses require those facts, not later core changes, and masking requires authorized Health delivery. Regression paths reach legacy false-positive states while the strengthened witnesses remain false. Diagnostics stutter the core; deliberately exposed private tags/counts and epoch bypass must fail." ; v:conditions "Same public action schedule, four imported core steps, one diagnostic delivery; private identity/existence are excluded from this profile's permitted operational disclosures." ; v:limit "No timing/resource/cache side-channel guarantee, anonymity or universal unlinkability; no retroactive revocation, physical erasure, legal compliance or complete LINDDUN analysis. Imported revocation changes epoch too, so isolated grant-check sensitivity is not established here." ; v:tracesTo v:REQ-12_5_3 .
